{"type":"item.completed","item":{"id":"item_3","type":"command_execution","command":"/bin/bash -lc \"python3 - <<'PY'\nimport json\np=json.load(open('../direct-checks/2a3711628c58423587c2ef66f2df64ee/plan.json'));p['harness'].pop('source');print(json.dumps(p,indent=2))\nPY\"","aggregated_output":"{\n  \"description\": \"Real-cluster VerifyLeader participant comparison with drained transport boundaries.\",\n  \"claim_id\": \"o-verify-voter-eligibility\",\n  \"binding_ids\": [\n    \"bind-verify-register\",\n    \"bind-verify-tally\",\n    \"bind-verify-result\",\n    \"bind-verify-producer\"\n  ],\n  \"harness\": {\n    \"files\": {},\n    \"kind\": \"go_test\",\n    \"description\": \"Two independent four-node histories: nonvoter-only released remote replies and voter-only control. Bootstrap, election, committed Apply and all-peer application prefix precede transport quiescence and public verification. Measure Error result and per-suffrage successful replies.\",\n    \"semantic_changes\": [\n      \"Embed InmemTransport and delay AppendEntries calls before real delivery using channels; do not change requests or responses.\",\n      \"Explicitly disable optional pipelining via ErrPipelineReplicationNotSupported; ordinary retry/fallback and heartbeat remain real.\",\n      \"Observe transport return fields and public futures; use MockFSM from captured testing support.\",\n      \"Cut schedule off after 600 ms independently of forbidden success; missing result remains unknown. Release all gates and shut down all nodes.\"\n    ],\n    \"prerequisites\": [\n      {\n        \"alias\": \"prefix\",\n        \"event\": \"prefix\",\n        \"conditions\": [\n          {\n            \"field\": \"voters\",\n            \"op\": \"eq\",\n            \"value\": 3,\n            \"reference\": null\n          },\n          {\n            \"field\": \"quiescent_loops\",\n            \"op\": \"eq\",\n            \"value\": 6,\n            \"reference\": null\n          }\n        ]\n      },\n      {\n        \"alias\": \"admission\",\n        \"event\": \"admitted\",\n        \"conditions\": [\n          {\n            \"field\": \"term\",\n            \"op\": \"eq\",\n            \"value\": null,\n            \"reference\": \"prefix.term\"\n          }\n        ]\n      }\n    ],\n    \"legality\": {\n      \"source_ids\": [\n        \"s-startup\",\n        \"s-bootstrap\",\n        \"s-config-change\",\n        \"s-repl-ownership\",\n        \"s-replication\",\n        \"s-heartbeat\",\n        \"s-rpc\",\n        \"s-transfer\",\n        \"s-inmem-transport-check\",\n        \"s-test-fsm-check\",\n        \"s-config-timing-check\",\n        \"s-getconfiguration-check\"\n      ],\n      \"expectation_ids\": [\n        \"s-transport-contract\",\n        \"s-verify-documentation\",\n        \"s-verify-api\"\n      ],\n      \"binding_ids\": [\n        \"bind-verify-register\",\n        \"bind-verify-tally\",\n        \"bind-verify-result\",\n        \"bind-verify-producer\"\n      ],\n      \"derivation\": \"BootstrapCluster/NewRaft start four real nodes with fixed configuration; node 0 wins an ordinary election and Apply completes. Each peer AppliedIndex reaches that prefix and leader CommitIndex covers the actual persisted bootstrap configuration entry, whose decoded membership matches GetConfiguration and the expected configuration. Only then does a wrapper pause calls before InmemTransport delivery. Pipelines report ErrPipelineReplicationNotSupported, a supported fallback. Both append and heartbeat loops for every peer must enter a paused next call before admission: their previous replies have already been consumed. Reset counters at that boundary. The selected peer is released after public VerifyLeader enqueue; all other replies remain delayed until result or the 600 ms cutoff. No RPC response, role, term, notification tally or stored protocol state is fabricated.\",\n      \"applicability\": \"Local test harness in package raft; actual target source unchanged. Controlled non-Byzantine finite delays with active normal workers and lease; peer election timeout exceeds experiment delay. New cluster per independent case, distinct op identity.\",\n      \"unresolved\": [\n        \"Scheduling that misses quiescence cutoff yields setup failure, not evidence. Missing verification completion emits only an incomplete diagnostic, not a result.\"\n      ],\n      \"conflicts\": [],\n      \"alternatives\": [\n        \"Voter lease can cause failure; it is not disabled or renewed artificially.\",\n        \"Negative responses from the released real peer are consumed normally. Unreleased responses are finitely delayed and all gates release during cleanup.\"\n      ]\n    }\n  },\n  \"monitors\": [\n    {\n      \"id\": \"monitor-verification\",\n      \"checker_id\": \"verify-voter-support\",\n      \"event\": \"result\",\n      \"binding_ids\": [\n        \"bind-verify-register\",\n        \"bind-verify-tally\",\n        \"bind-verify-result\",\n        \"bind-verify-producer\"\n      ],\n      \"grounding\": {\n        \"source_ids\": [\n          \"s-leader-loop\",\n          \"s-repl-ownership\",\n          \"s-verify-vote\",\n          \"s-replication\",\n          \"s-heartbeat\",\n          \"s-transfer\"\n        ],\n        \"expectation_ids\": [\n          \"s-verify-documentation\",\n          \"s-verify-api\",\n          \"s-membership-contract\",\n          \"s-verify-tests\"\n        ],\n        \"binding_ids\": [\n          \"bind-verify-register\",\n          \"bind-verify-tally\",\n          \"bind-verify-result\",\n          \"bind-verify-producer\"\n        ],\n        \"derivation\": \"A successful verification requires eligible remote support in a three-voter configuration. The checker uses success implies at least one observed remote voter positive reply after all earlier sender loops have drained. In the forbidden schedule both remote voter loops remain gated, so no remote voter can submit a new notification; only the nonvoter is released. In the control only a voter is released. Reply counts are measured by the transport after real receiver processing, not preset expected outcomes.\",\n        \"applicability\": \"Real election and committed application prefix, fixed three-voter/one-nonvoter membership, same operation ID across prefix/admission/result; no state assignments. Pipeline-disabled supported transport variant. Finite request delays, real peer receivers, active lease and all Raft workers.\",\n        \"unresolved\": [\n          \"A result proves the local participant-eligibility proposition only. No competing authority or stale application read is observed.\",\n          \"Successful reply count is an upper bound on consumed support; absence proves no voter consumption after quiescence. The permitted control releases only the voter, excluding nonvoter substitution.\"\n        ],\n        \"conflicts\": [],\n        \"alternatives\": [\n          \"Lease may terminate the old leader later, but does not qualify an earlier nonvoter contribution.\",\n          \"Negative support can reject verification; schedule must preserve or finitely delay this path and report its handling.\",\n          \"Current authority might in fact persist despite lost communication; the obligation constrains verification support rather than asserting a competing leader.\"\n        ]\n      },\n      \"applicability_conditions\": [],\n      \"admission_alias\": \"admission\"\n    }\n  ],\n  \"observable_properties\": [\n    {\n      \"checker_id\": \"verify-voter-support\",\n      \"kind\": \"event_implication\",\n      \"trigger\": {\n        \"field\": \"event\",\n        \"op\": \"eq\",\n        \"value\": \"result\",\n        \"reference\": null\n      },\n      \"assertion\": {\n        \"field\": \"remote_voter_reply\",\n        \"op\": \"eq\",\n        \"value\": true,\n        \"reference\": null\n      },\n      \"antecedent\": {\n        \"field\": \"success\",\n        \"op\": \"eq\",\n        \"value\": true,\n        \"reference\": null\n      },\n      \"identity_fields\": [\n        \"op\"\n      ],\n      \"history_field\": null,\n      \"description\": \"Success implies an observed positive remote voter reply since the quiescent boundary. Nonvoter-only completion violates the necessary participant eligibility condition; no success is required of a pending operation.\"\n    }\n  ],\n  \"uncertainties\": [\n    \"No broader stale-read or later-leader endpoint is measured.\",\n    \"Counts are transport delivery observations, not instrumentation inside vote(); absence of any eligible reply after complete two-loop quiescence is the relevant discriminator.\",\n    \"An independently missing case is reported incomplete and cannot supply a holds result.\"\n  ]\n}\n","exit_code":0,"status":"completed"}}
{"type":"item.completed","item":{"id":"item_4","type":"agent_message","text":"The runner recorded a complete violating witness: `VerifyLeader` returned success with three nonvoter replies and zero remote-voter replies after the drain boundary. The voter control also completed successfully. The fixed harness establishes the election and committed prefix through real workers; it does not establish a competing leader or stale application read. I’ll record those limits in the review and compare the remaining leads."}}
{"type":"item.started","item":{"id":"item_5","type":"command_execution","command":"/bin/bash -lc \"cat > build_review.py <<'PY'\nimport json\nss=['s-verify-documentation','s-verify-api','s-membership-contract','s-verify-tests','s-leader-loop','s-repl-ownership','s-verify-vote','s-replication','s-heartbeat','s-match-notify','s-transfer','s-startup','s-bootstrap','s-rpc','s-inmem-transport-check','s-config-timing-check','s-test-fsm-check','s-getconfiguration-check','s-dispatch','s-future-completion']\nitems=[dict(aspect='applicability',status='no_issue_found',source_ids=ss,rationale='The accepted proposition is a participant-eligibility condition on verification, not a claim that lack of communication instantly removes authority. s-verify-documentation explicitly assigns VerifyLeader confirmation to voters; s-verify-api says it ensures leadership and may prevent stale FSM reads. s-membership-contract separates nonvoters from election/commitment participants. s-verify-tests includes success with one disconnected peer among three voters, so neither unanimity nor eventual success is demanded. s-leader-loop and s-transfer implement a majority calculated only from voters. Three voters plus one nonvoter is a validated ordinary configuration (s-config-timing-check, s-bootstrap, s-repl-ownership), not forced recovery. Real bootstrap/election/application establish the selected context. No conflicting source authorizes nonvoter substitution for the missing voter in verification.',counterevidence=[],limitations=['The expectation is the narrow implementation verification contract derived from documentation and API, not a complete formal definition of linearizable reads.','This execution does not show loss of actual leadership; absence of eligible verification support is the checked discrepancy.']),dict(aspect='decomposition',status='no_issue_found',source_ids=ss,rationale='The consumer obligation is necessary, not sufficient for authority safety. b-verify starts at self=1 and threshold=2, registers all peer workers (s-leader-loop); b-heartbeat and b-notify-replication drain a future registration into Boolean vote without suffrage (s-replication, s-match-notify). With both remote voter send loops paused before delivery and prior replies consumed, no voter can supply a notification for the new future. Only released nonvoter workers can provide the missing positive notification. The voter-only control reaches the same public endpoint. Freshness of replies, concurrent membership changes and authority loss might still invalidate a verification even when voter eligibility holds, and are separate conditions. Lease failure and negative replies remain valid rejection paths: main loop and timer run, only peer calls are finitely delayed, and the released receiver responses are not altered.',counterevidence=[],limitations=['Cannot distinguish which nonvoter positive reply—ordinary append or heartbeat—first drained this registration. Both are sourced producers of the same Boolean fact, and the participant conclusion does not require isolating them.','Transport positive counts are an upper bound on consumed positive notifications; absence is sufficient for this forbidden schedule but arbitrary positive counts would not prove quorum consumption.']),dict(aspect='checker_correspondence',status='no_issue_found',source_ids=ss,rationale='Inspected the fixed v1 plan and assurance_generated_test.go under direct-checks/2a3711628c58423587c2ef66f2df64ee and raw execution a5644db0464f44ccb5dfc352dcff28b0. The driver creates fresh stores and real NewRaft workers, bootstraps identical membership, waits for actual node-0 election and successful Apply, reads persisted LogConfiguration index 1, compares decoded and public membership, and requires CommitIndex to cover that entry. It does not rely on GetConfiguration().Index(), whose implementation returns a configuration without its index (s-getconfiguration-check). Peer AppliedIndex is only queued-application progress per s-dispatch; completed remote FSM application is unnecessary to participant eligibility. Pipelines are explicitly unsupported, leaving one serial append and one serial heartbeat loop per peer (s-replication, s-heartbeat). The gate records each loop only at its next call before delivery, so the preceding response and notifyAll invocation have completed; all six gates remain closed until admission. No snapshots are triggered in this short, non-compacted three-entry history and no other RPC supplies verifyFuture votes. Thus reset counters cannot erase an outstanding voter response capable of later notifying this future. The public VerifyLeader call precedes the admitted event; only the selected peer gate then opens. Actual receiver code fills response fields, wrapper counts positive successful returns by independent ServerID, and future.Error supplies success. Result event is not a prerequisite. The monitor explicitly admits via admission, correlates independent op identity, and requires prefix.term before admission.term; it does not equate changing state with identity. The implication success => remote_voter_reply avoids demanding success of a pending operation. Raw events 0/1/2 identify nonvoter prefix/admission/result with term 2, persisted configuration index 1, command index 3, success=true, voter_replies=0 and nonvoter_replies=3; state remains Leader. Events 3/4/5 independently identify the voter control: success=true, voter_replies=3 and nonvoter_replies=0. Both scenarios complete, parsing has no errors, and the runner evaluated both result events with matching prerequisites. Later command-timeout logs occur after result during release/shutdown, not in the violating identity before observation. The independent 600 ms cutoff, setup deadlines, deferred releases and shutdown do not depend on observing forbidden success. No_issue_found is scoped correspondence review of this actual artifact, not an independent proof or a general validation of the implementation.',counterevidence=[],limitations=['Only the no-pipeline in-memory transport variant with finite selective delays and unchanged membership is executed.','Public successful verification is observed; a subsequent FSM read, competing leader election and committed-data inconsistency are not.','The source basis explains nonvoter notification consumption, but this test is not an isolated comparison of every potential cause of stale verification.'])]\nsub=dict(action='review',artifact_id='ded691143aa74e5fbdc74fdcf6724f41',rationale='Review the fixed check, legal real-worker prefix, absence-of-voter-support argument and actual public result together. The measured violation is attributable to the accepted participant-eligibility proposition within its declared scope.',review_items=items,feedback=dict(ref_ids=['ded691143aa74e5fbdc74fdcf6724f41','a5644db0464f44ccb5dfc352dcff28b0','s-leader-loop','s-repl-ownership','s-replication','s-heartbeat','s-verify-vote'],answered='The trusted run answered the local question: a real verification future completed successfully using only nonvoter remote replies after all prior voter responses were drained. Both required schedules completed. Real bootstrap/election, committed prefix, actual reply producers and public Error endpoint replace the proposal-time construction gaps. The existing map already expresses the reusable all-peer registration and Boolean consumption relationship, so this conditional execution result remains in its evidence records rather than becoming a broader code fact.',remaining=['No competing authority or stale application read endpoint has been observed.','The notification path also leaves reply freshness and generation/registration timing questions outside this completed participant check.'],understanding='updated',rationale='Return to the overview: voter eligibility is now locally measured, while reply context and pipeline support remain untested. Compare (1) broader stale-read consequence: high consequence but needs a correlated new election and application endpoint; (2) heartbeat higher-term/contact asymmetry: active lease and normal replication complicate a meaningful safety/deadline oracle; (3) pipeline completion error consumption: explicit AppendFuture.Response interface requirement, a concrete producer publishing error futures, and an unguarded consumer directly updating commit support. Prefer source investigation of option (3) next to determine whether an allowed transport error can expose apparently positive partial response fields, before deriving any new obligation. Preserve option (1) as a separate consequence question; do not reopen the completed local eligibility proposition.',question_updates={'49ce55feb3334fb6bb71c5b6e7ebc09f':dict(unknowns=['Broader stale-read or competing-leader consequence is outside this checked proposition.','This witness identifies nonvoter substitution but not which of the peer heartbeat/ordinary-append callbacks first supplied it.'],resume_conditions=[])}))\njson.dump(sub,open('verify-review.json','w'),indent=2)\nPY\npython3 build_review.py\npython3 - <<'PY'\nimport json,subprocess\nr=json.load(open('../research.json'));p=subprocess.run(r['validation']['command']+['verify-review.json'],capture_output=True,text=True);print(p.stdout)\nPY\"","aggregated_output":"","exit_code":null,"status":"in_progress"}}
